From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Moritz=20Mei=C3=9Felbach?= <moritz@glassine.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:38:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] freedreno/a5xx: no 2D blitter on the A509 (blits write
 nothing)

On the Adreno 509 (Boox Note Air 1, Mesa 25.1.9) fd5_blitter_blit's CP_BLIT
completes without a fault and leaves the destination unchanged:

- texture uploads into a texture the GPU still references (staging BO +
  fd_blit_from_staging) are lost, at every size (64x64 to 1872x1404) and in
  R32UI and RGBA8; with the staging path forced for idle textures too, the
  first full upload is lost as well;
- glCopyBufferSubData (emit_blit_buffer) leaves the destination buffer as it
  was (4 KiB to 256 KiB, aligned and unaligned offsets).

A WFI after END2D, CCU color/depth flushes plus a UCHE flush after the blit,
and RB_DBG_ECO_CNTL bit 9 (the kernel's 1-SP clock-gating workaround, which
fd5_emit_restore overwrites) each and together change nothing.
FD_MESA_DEBUG=noblit (u_blitter on the 3D pipe) gets all of them right, so do
the same for the A509 without the env var. Other a5xx parts are untouched
(a530 CI passes the 2D path).

Test: an upload probe (full|part|small, sync 0, R32UI/RGBA8; bufcopy):
stock 8/8 and 6/6 wrong, patched 0 wrong, 0 GPU faults.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (unreviewed; tested only on the A509)
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_context.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_context.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_context.c
index 3fda7cb5320..eb1500fe467 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_context.c
@@ -74,7 +74,12 @@ fd5_context_create(struct pipe_screen *pscreen, void *priv,
    fd5_prog_init(pctx);
    fd5_emit_init(pctx);
 
-   if (!FD_DBG(NOBLIT))
+   /* The 2D engine (CP_BLIT) writes nothing on the A509: texture and buffer
+    * blits complete without a fault and leave the destination unchanged,
+    * idle or busy, with or without a WFI and CCU/cache flushes after the
+    * blit.  Use the 3D path (u_blitter) there instead.
+    */
+   if (!FD_DBG(NOBLIT) && screen->gpu_id != 509)
       fd5_ctx->base.blit = fd5_blitter_blit;
 
    pctx = fd_context_init(&fd5_ctx->base, pscreen, priv, flags);
